{
  "_comment": [
    "Photo -> room map for the walkthrough. build.py mounts each photo on a wall",
    "of its room, so only 'at' and the photo list matter.",
    "'at' is [x, z] in the scene frame build.py prints (metres, +X east, +Z south,",
    "origin at the footprint centre). Levels are 0 = Downstairs, 1 = Upstairs.",
    "Room names, and which bedroom a photo belongs to, are a reading of the scan,",
    "not something RoomPlan recorded — edit freely.",
    "Optional \"floorFrom\": \"<room>\" borrows another room's floor, for a room",
    "photographed from its doorway that shows no floor of its own.",
    "One photo may carry \"view\" and \"ground\" — [x, y, w, h] in 0..1 of that",
    "picture — naming the crop the world outside the windows is built from.",
    "Top-level 'finishes' are every room's defaults and a room's own win. A wall or",
    "ceiling may name a paint as '#rrggbb'; a floor may name a wood or tile from the",
    "palette in src/photo/relight.js (timber-white-oak, tile-porcelain) and is laid",
    "from the palette rather than sampled. 'furnishings' maps a scanned category to",
    "a product in src/scene/products.js. 'kitchen' and 'bath' lay out a room; see",
    "src/scene/kitchen.js and src/scene/bath.js for their shape."
  ],
